WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.900 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The homepage lists three
paths for paper orders.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:13.467 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The search dialog finds
the troubleshooting guide.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.900 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The lab opens from
the site navigation.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.033 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The ZIP includes a script
and three sample records.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:23.833 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The Node.js example
prints 0 of 10 filled.

00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:30.867 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The tabs switch among
three states of one order.

00:00:30.867 --> 00:00:33.900 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
Three squares stay filled
when the order is canceled.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:40.000 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The JSON shows qty, status
and filled_qty.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.467 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The troubleshooting guide
opens on cancellation.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:47.533 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The reply asks for the ID
to check the actual order.

00:00:47.533 --> 00:00:51.900 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The link opens the
read-only lookup by ID.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.033 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The second lookup accepts
the saved client_order_id.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:59.900 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The guide explains what
a 404 leaves unresolved.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.367 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The teaching article opens
on the three-page project.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:08.867 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The article shows the
scaffold and seed files.

00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:17.900 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The instructions identify
the page and its heading.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:24.033 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
A tabs example sets up
the guide navigation.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:27.900 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The helper prints the rank,
link and returned text.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.233 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The final section covers
self-hosting and Cloud.

00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:38.033 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The example site offers
page and section search.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:41.867 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The first section answers
the cancellation question.

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:46.867 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The search field gets
a different question.

00:01:46.867 --> 00:01:49.167 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The first section names
the writer’s test steps.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.733 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The recorded learner result
appears below live search.

00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:56.200 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The example wrongly uses
the sample’s three fills.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:01.500 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The draft stays in the tab.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:09.400 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
Two canceled fixtures have
different fill counts.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.867 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The appendix compares
source with served copy.

00:02:11.867 --> 00:02:18.300 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The last two checks cover
MCP output and the ZIP.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.367 line:76% position:50% size:91% align:center
The agent reference opens
